+# Synchronous focus cancellation ownership repair
+
+Base candidate: `2b5eaa0b0db6ef12882a38b6cd143291144d4150`.
+Independent rejection: `372eb7de549492021520db38c3c51459ab4d982d`.
+
+Publish first-down ownership before calling renderer.handleKeyDown, which can synchronously invoke callbacks after physical state and DOWN have been recorded. Preserve first metadata across repeats. If cancellation or a replacement ownership occurs while delivery is on stack, the outer invocation stops before emitting stale character input. An exception from delivery leaves ownership available for a later up/cancellation: the bridge cannot know how far a throwing renderer progressed and does not attempt to roll back renderer state.
+
+Cancellation snapshots ownership identities, deletes each before calling out, and skips ownership already consumed/replaced by nested callbacks. A throwing release is remembered while other snapshot owners are released; the first thrown value is propagated afterward. Release is attempted exactly once per owner. This does not promise recovery when an arbitrary renderer throws before it changes physical state, nor does it drain fresh keydown events deliberately dispatched after a cancellation snapshot. Renderer and guest semantics remain unchanged.
+
+Validation used serial `timeout 25s node --max-old-space-size=16` commands recorded in checkpoint.json: unchanged supplied 19/19, unchanged independent 7/7, scoped repair 6/6. The independent callback now observes hidden=true, physical=0 and queue DOWN/UP. Scoped tests cover nested actual-renderer downs/repeats/cancellation, nested cancellation during release, replacement ownership, throwing actual queue publishers, and stale printable input after cancellation. The scoped DOM/renderer helper derives from the pinned independent helper; its independent oracle is unchanged and is a local untracked validation input, never committed on this task branch.
+
+Original candidate/parent narrow failure logs, original supplied parent failure and original input pins are retained byte-for-byte here. They establish an existing defect through a controlled callback seam; this report does not claim current host callbacks routinely hide documents. pins.json binds exact tested repair source, unchanged sources/oracles and scoped test. evidence-manifest.json seals other report payloads; ops/result.json records final commit/publication separately.
+
+Only lib/browser-input.js, the owned regression and this report directory are committed. No main integration, independent acceptance decision, full build, browser/runtime/gameplay qualification, services, Boat or boxes. Box ID/state/expiry: N/A; coordinator retains lifecycle ownership. No workers were spawned. Root and donor checkouts/index/refs stayed readonly; the shared messageboard was append-only. Resource receipts separately identify standing tools/read-only inputs and count checkout/Git/evidence, launcher/session/WAL/future growth once plus reserve.
+
+Recovery: borrow unchanged local donor objects listed in the isolated .git/objects/info/alternates, or fetch task/browser-key-reentrant-focus-ownership-repair-oct26 from the trusted origin into a new checkout. Run the supplied and scoped tests there with the commands in checkpoint.json. Recover the independent fixture byte-exact from review commit 372eb7de549492021520db38c3c51459ab4d982d and verify pins.json before its command. No ignored binary or guest artifact is required. Do not use this task as main publication authorization.
